<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37034" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Popĭlĭus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Popill-</span></b> ), i,
		m., and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Popi-lĭa</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Popill-</span></b> ), ae, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the name of a
			Roman</i> gens. So esp., </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> M. Popillius Laenas, <i>a consul</i> A.
			U.C. 395, <i><span class="en">Cic. Brut. 14,
			56</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			C. Popilius Laenas, <i>the assassin of Cicero</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Liv. Epit. 120</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Suas.
				7</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> In <i>fem.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Popilia,</span>”
				<i>the wife of Q. Catulus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					de Or. 2, 11, 44</span></i>
			.— Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Popĭlĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to a Popilius</i>, <i>Popilian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Leg. 2, 22, 55</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
